{{!
    Overrides the auth block that common_README.mustache pulls into Getting
    Started. Only this partial is overridden, so the endpoint, model and
    authorization tables still come from the jar.

    NOTE: a mustache comment ends at its first closing brace pair, so no
    variable or partial tag may appear in this block.

    Three defects in the built-in partial motivated the override. It calls
    os.environ without importing os, so the snippet raises NameError as
    printed; common_README imports only the package, ApiException and pprint.
    It assigns `configuration` twice, so the host set in the first assignment
    is silently discarded by the second. And it reads USERNAME and PASSWORD,
    which is wrong for this API -- the key goes in the password field with an
    empty username, and USERNAME is a real shell variable on most systems, so
    the example would quietly send the caller's login name.

    The branches for bearer, API-key, OAuth and HTTP-signature auth are
    dropped: this spec declares only HTTP basic.
}}
# Authentication is HTTP basic, with your API key in the password field and an
# empty username. The key has the form "<keyId>.<secret>".
#
# The host defaults to {{{basePath}}}. Pass host= to target another server.
# See configuration.py for all supported parameters.
import os

configuration = {{{packageName}}}.Configuration(
    username = "",
    password = os.environ["DDX_API_KEY"],
)
